# The role-actuator service of a Docker host's Compose project (templates/docker-compose.role-actuator.yml.j2): bash, jq, flock and the Docker CLI with its Compose and Buildx plugins, all from Alpine's apk, Buildx because Compose builds a service's image with it, which the first start of a service the host has never run needs. flock is util-linux's, since BusyBox's takes no timeout (-w), which the actuator's switch lock (lock_switch in fleet-role-actuator-docker.sh) waits with. date is BusyBox's. No kubectl: the actuator runs the kubectl of the node container that is up (node_kubectl in fleet-role-actuator-docker.sh), since only the node containers are on the tailnet the API servers are reached over. The scripts it runs are not copied in: the service mounts the project directory, which holds them, so a host picks up a collection upgrade when the service is created again, without an image Compose would not otherwise rebuild.
FROM alpine:3.22

RUN apk add --no-cache bash jq flock docker-cli docker-cli-compose docker-cli-buildx
